DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ccggggeett(), ccggrreeaadd(), and ccggrreeaadd11() functions provide cylinder group
     reads for libufs(3) consumers.  The ccggppuutt(), ccggwwrriittee(), and ccggwwrriittee11()
     functions provide cylinder group writes for libufs(3) consumers.

     The ccggggeett() function reads the cylinder group specified by _c_g into the
     buffer pointed to by _c_g_p from the filesystem described by the _f_s su‐
     perblock using the _d_e_v_f_d file descriptor that references the filesystem
     disk.  The ccggggeett() function is the only cylinder group read function that
     is safe to use in threaded applications.

     The ccggppuutt() function writes the cylinder group specified by _c_g_p to the
     filesystem described by the _f_s superblock using the _d_e_v_f_d file descriptor
     that references the filesystem disk.  The ccggppuutt() function is the only
     cylinder group write function that is safe to use in threaded applica‐
     tions.  Note that the ccggppuutt() function needs to be called only if the
     cylinder group has been modified and the on-disk copy needs to be up‐
     dated.

     The ccggrreeaadd11() function reads from the cylinder group specified by _c_g into
     the _d___c_g cylinder-group structure in a user-land UFS-disk structure.  It
     sets the _d___l_c_g field to the cylinder group number _c_g.

     The ccggrreeaadd() function operates on sequential cylinder groups.  Calling
     the ccggrreeaadd() function is equivalent to calling ccggrreeaadd11() with a cylinder
     group specifier equivalent to the value of the current _d___c_c_g field, and
     then incrementing the _d___c_c_g field.

     The ccggwwrriittee() function stores on disk the cylinder group held in the _d___c_g
     cylinder-group structure in a user-land UFS-disk structure.

     The ccggwwrriittee11() function provides no additional functionality over the
     ccggwwrriittee() function as there is only one place that a given cylinder group
     can correctly be written.  If the caller gets the _c_g parameter wrong, the
     function fails with the error EDOOFUS.  This function remains only to
     provide backward compatibility.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ccggrreeaadd() function returns 0 if there are no more cylinder groups to
     read, 1 if there are more cylinder groups, and -1 on error.  The
     ccggrreeaadd11() function returns 1 on success and -1 on error.  The other func‐
     tions return 0 on success and -1 on error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The ccggggeett(), ccggrreeaadd(), and ccggrreeaadd11() functions may fail and set _e_r_r_n_o for
     any of the errors specified for the library function bread(3).

     The ccggppuutt(), ccggwwrriittee(), and ccggwwrriittee11() functions may fail and set _e_r_r_n_o
     for any of the errors specified for the library function bwrite(3).  Ad‐
     ditionally the ccggwwrriittee11() will return the EDOOFUS error if the cylinder
     group specified does not match the cylinder group that it is requesting
     to write.

